<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - May 3.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - May 3.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended May 3</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   310	   0.76     489050  151.61   12.78</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    220	   0.55     180350   39.68   13.04</p>
<p>Colgate		305	   0.74     108450   33.08   12.65</p>
<p>ACC		   1430	   3.34	22530   32.22   12.18</p>
<p>Castrol		425	   1.09	68650   29.18   13.37</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   885	   2.21	26050   23.05   13.02</p>
<p>Century Textiles  2430	   6.14	 8970   21.80   13.18</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 131	   0.33     160350   21.01   13.14</p>
<p>HDFC		  3145	  97.93	 4800   15.10   40.59</p>
<p>Tata Power	   140	   0.28	92000   12.88   10.43</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 14.43 percent on an annualised basis against 13.36 % in the previous carry forward account ended April 26</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
